w: 1.~The earth be- longs un- to the Lord, and all that it con- tains; _ The world that is in- ha- bi- ted, and all that there re- mains.
w: 2.~For the foun- da- ti- ons there- of he on the seas did lay, _ And he hath it e- sta- blish- èd up- on the floods to stay.
w: 3.~Who is the man that shall a- scend in- to the hill of God? _ Or who with- in his ho- ly place shall have a firm a- bode?
w: 4.~Whose hands are clean, whose heart is pure, and un- to va- ni- ty _ Who hath not lift- ed up his soul, nor sworn de- ceit- ful- ly.
w: 5.~He from th'E- ter- nal shall re- ceive the bless- ing him up- on, _ And right- eous- ness, ev'n from the God of his sal- va- ti- on.
w: 6.~This is the ge- ne- ra- ti- on that af- ter him en- quire, _ O Ja- cob, who do seek thy face with their whole heart's de- sire.
w: 7.~Ye gates, lift up your heads on high; ye doors that last for aye, _ Be lift- ed up, that so the King of glo- ry en- ter may.
w: 8.~But who of glo- ry is the King? The might- y Lord is this; _ Ev'n that same Lord, that great in might and strong in bat- tle is.
w: 9.~Ye gates, lift up your heads; ye doors, doors that do last for aye, _ Be lift- ed up, that so the King of glo- ry en- ter may.
w: 10.~But who is he that is the King of glo- ry? who is this? _ The Lord of hosts, and none but he, the King of glo- ry is.
